{"id":"1b528408f2c37ce3","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-thm-measure-properties.md","title":"Measure Properties","display":"thm-measure-properties — Measure Properties","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-measure-properties","aliases":["58-thm-measure-properties","Measure Theory Properties","Lebesgue Measure Properties"],"display":"thm-measure-properties — Measure Properties","depends_on":["[[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-measure-properties"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-measure-properties</span><span>Measure Theory Properties</span><span>Lebesgue Measure Properties</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-measure-properties — Measure Properties"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"68427bc628af9b8d\" href=\"?note=68427bc628af9b8d\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue\">../batch10/58-df-lebesgue</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> (Lebesgue measure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"68427bc628af9b8d\" href=\"?note=68427bc628af9b8d\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue\">../batch10/58-df-lebesgue</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L\">\\(\\mathcal L\\)</span> (Lebesgue <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">\\(\\sigma\\)</span>-algebra)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in\\mathcal L\">\\(A\\in\\mathcal L\\)</span> (Lebesgue-measurable set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\\in\\mathbb R\">\\(x\\in\\mathbb R\\)</span> (translation vector)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S\\)</span> (three-place Lebesgue-measure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"68427bc628af9b8d\" href=\"?note=68427bc628af9b8d\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue\">../batch10/58-df-lebesgue</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}measure\\text{-}properties} \\vdash \\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\mu,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\to\\forall A\\in\\mathcal L\\;\\forall x\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\bigl(A+x\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\mu(A+x)=\\mu(A)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}measure\\text{-}properties} \\vdash \\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\mu,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\to\\forall A\\in\\mathcal L\\;\\forall x\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\bigl(A+x\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\mu(A+x)=\\mu(A)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Lebesgue: developed measure theory (1902).</li>\n<li>Translation-invariance: key property for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Regularity: approximation by nice sets.</li>\n<li>Completion: all null sets included.</li>\n<li>Fubini: product integration.</li>\n<li>Regularity and completion are part of the standard Lebesgue package, and Fubini describes the product behavior.</li>\n<li>Banach-Tarski: shows non-measurable sets exist (using AC).</li>\n<li>The upstream atom formalizes one-dimensional Lebesgue measure with signature <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\mu,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\">\\((\\mu,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\)</span>; no unsupported <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\mathbb R^n\\)</span> overload is used here.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue","status":"resolved","id":"68427bc628af9b8d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue","status":"resolved","id":"68427bc628af9b8d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mu$ (Lebesgue measure on $\\mathbb R$, see [[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue","status":"resolved","id":"68427bc628af9b8d","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S$ (three-place Lebesgue-measure predicate, see [[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal L","display":false},{"tex":"\\sigma","display":false},{"tex":"A\\in\\mathcal L","display":false},{"tex":"x\\in\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}measure\\text{-}properties} \\vdash \\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\mu,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\to\\forall A\\in\\mathcal L\\;\\forall x\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\bigl(A+x\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\mu(A+x)=\\mu(A)\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"(\\mu,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R^n","display":false}],"bytes":1482,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4309","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-thm-measure-properties.md|58-thm-measure-properties]]（batch12）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-217","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-thm-0-sharp.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-condensation.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-definability.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-generic-extension.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-is-transitive.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-s